    {
      "id": "claim_e035a251aa564bb3bf9bf5451f7bd02f",
      "statement": "Deletes are soft: Delete and DeleteByPath set s_state = 'DELETED' and stamp d_delete = NOW() instead of removing rows, and every read path filters s_state != 'DELETED', so a deleted key behaves as absent and its path/subkey pair can be re-created with version 1 while tombstones remain for audit.",
